{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "M",
  "theme": "mdash",
  "_about": "M-style cluster traced 1:1 off a photo of a current M8's cluster (design/photos/ref-m8-cluster.png, warped to 1920x720 and measured on the pixels Nov 6 2026; generated by design/gen_m.py, edit that): black, a near-black card either side whose top edge is the photo's curve, bowed glass rev blades (the photo's curve, 0..7000 rpm, the M40i's own scale) with a red marker block riding the rpm, the gear with its shifter programme (P, D3, S3, M3) and the speed in white over the centre line, the tyre pressure and temperature block on the left (TPMS in the car's own units, polled every 10 s; '--' until the car answers), the setup rows on the right (Eco Pro, Comfort, Sport, Sport Plus, Individual), the fuel and oil dials over the cards' lower corners, range, the clock and the outside temperature along the bottom. Backdrop, tyre glyph, dials and the setup level bars are one shader (mdash); the rev bars are mtach: 3 effect layers plus the text sheets. Deviations from the photo, all forced by the X3: the setup rows are split round the black box BMW draws at x 1406..1597, y 342..419 (two above, two below; the M8 stacks all four there); the badge is the M stripes without the M8 text; the clock ends before BMW's belt light (x 587). Fuel and range from KombiIF statusRangeTankStatus (config.tankLitres is the full mark), outside temperature from EnvironmentalInformation. No speed limit sign: no app has found that signal yet. 'Leave room for the map' is not supported in this theme. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
